# Ambling Stormshell: "Whenever you cast a Turtle spell, untap this creature." After it attacks with three stun counters,
# Bot1 casts an Aegis Turtle in its second main phase: the untap would happen, so one stun counter is removed instead (CR
# 122.1d) and the Stormshell stays tapped with two. A Mox Ruby cast first is no Turtle: it changes nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Ambling Stormshell
Aegis Turtle
Mox Ruby
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Ambling Stormshell.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ambling Stormshell > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ambling Stormshell.Counters.Stun = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Aegis Turtle.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ambling Stormshell.Counters.Stun = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ambling Stormshell.Tapped = true
